\cf2 \cb7 So I think the stronger, defensible reworking is:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 Fourfold phase structure describes how differentiation acts within a harmonic representation. Causality constrains which combinations of those representations correspond to admissible physical responses.
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 The two structures interact.\cf0 \cb1 \
