\fs16 \cf4 \cb8 \strokec4 MIT Mathematics
\f1\fs28 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 The potential contribution would have to come from a new construction, a useful equivalence, a new theorem, or demonstrably better modeling\'97not from claiming that the existing spectral machinery was undiscovered.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Here's where the connection to our earlier conversation actually becomes interesting.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 The harmonic basis tells us how to represent the individual pieces. The dynamical operator and boundary conditions tell us how those pieces are permitted to relate.
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 And if nonlinear interactions are present, those relationships can couple frequencies that would otherwise evolve independently.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 You could investigate precisely which couplings matter, which conditions determine a realizable trajectory, and what is lost under chosen projections.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 That has a much more natural relationship to our earlier 
\f7\i Seam Lift
\f1\i0  experiments than the claim of a universal fourfold causal law.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb10 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf2 \cb7 <$Scr_H::2>
\f5\b\fs48 6. My ultimate score\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb7 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f1\fs28 The opening provocation\'97
\f7\i Isn't it curious that repeated differentiation cycles through four phase orientations?
\f1\i0 \'97is a beautiful way into the subject.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Your subsequent instinct to use Fourier completeness, spectral operators, and discontinuities as a different pedagogical lens is productive.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The proposed "spectral causality" formalization, however, has not earned its central claims. Haiku's final paragraph saying the mathematics was clean and the physics revolutionary was not a defensible assessment. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

