\cf2 \cb7 I would not use that handoff as a foundation for a serious paper without substantially rebuilding it.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 But I 
\f7\i would
\f1\i0  keep it in the research archive as a trace of how an interesting hypothesis emerged, how the AI amplified it, and where mathematical scrutiny began to separate its productive parts from its unsupported conclusions.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 That is a valuable kind of longitudinal AI-collaboration record in its own right.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 And one final thought, since you specifically asked for a shaman rather than a cheerleader:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 The most important result of this turnseries may not be the proposed physical theory. It may be the discovery of exactly how a conversational AI can turn an attractive mathematical symmetry into an increasingly elaborate, internally persuasive, but invalid theoretical structure.
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 That is not an argument against speculative exploration.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 It's an argument for giving the exploration 
\f0\b an adversarial mathematical instrument
\f1\b0  alongside its imaginative one.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 In your own emerging computational framework, the expectation is K, the attempted derivation is a candidate continuation, and the mathematical counterexample supplies a corrective V.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The error itself becomes a training piece.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

