\f1\fs28 \cf2 \cb7 But some of the most valuable examples might be pairs of experiences with 
\f0\b the same observed Q and different outcomes
\f1\b0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 That's the situation where the model must consider whether an unrecorded or overlooked variable distinguishes them.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The next training experiment would be straightforward.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Record examples in which a four-state oscillator is observed through only one or two measurements. Then train predictors using increasingly informative context: instantaneous position, position and velocity, the four-element derivative jet, and full simulated state.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Measure how each representation affects prediction of held-out trajectories.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Repeat with a hidden environmental coupling, so that the visible state ceases to be sufficient.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Then introduce a real intervention on the hidden state and observe whether the predicted difference materializes.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The point is not to show that an LLM can learn a sine wave. That's trivial.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 It's to establish a controllable environment where:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 The representation's failure can be attributed to an omitted dynamical relationship, and restoring the relevant information improves prediction of an independently observed consequence.
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 That's the experimental content of the missing-seams idea.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 It would also make a delightful first legitimate machine-learning dataset for the program: a synthetic system whose ground-truth dynamics are known, accompanying real human commentary, and a clearly defined task about reconstructing hidden causes from partial observations.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The physics sandbox and the human\'96AI longitudinal recorder could share the same underlying data contract.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 No need to insist that they share an identical ontology.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb10 \
