\f1\fs28 \cf2 \cb7 This system has a genuine fourfold derivative cycle.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 It can be represented using real coordinates, complex coordinates, or the octonionic cross product.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 And now the mathematics isn't merely a metaphor about causal closure. We've constructed actual differential equations.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 This model is not new physics; it's a particular rotation generated by a chosen skew-symmetric operator.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 But it's an 
\f0\b exact reference system
\f1\b0  in which your proposed connections among dimensionality, complex phase, cross-product structure, and differential cyclicity coexist without contradiction.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 A richer model could introduce forcing, environmental couplings, observation projections, and nonlinear terms.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Then we'd investigate which of the fourfold structures survive those extensions.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 That's how I'd turn the provocation into a research program.\cf0 \cb1 \
