\f1\fs28 I want to distinguish the counterfactual from what actually happened.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 My first critique of Haiku was correct about several specific claims. The original four sinusoidal functions weren't four independent basis elements; its Gibbs interpretation wasn't a general causal law; its dissipation arguments were too sweeping.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 But my critique did not sufficiently pursue the most constructive alternative:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 What ambient algebra, state space, or observation geometry would make the proposed phase structure genuinely useful?
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 My next reconstruction began asking that question through a four-dimensional lifted state space.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 Your seven-dimensional stipulation now supplies another candidate, with an established and exceptional algebraic structure.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 So the answer is:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb7 I would have rejected the derivation as written. I should not have rejected the underlying research direction. And I would not have required you to prove the entire conceptual framework before exploring a new mathematical representation.
\f1\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 The Haiku cutoff doesn't substantially change that judgment. The important mathematics was already available well before July 2025. Its failures were not primarily failures of recency, but failures of inference discipline and calibration.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb7 The deeper mistake would have been confusing:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f7\i \cf2 \cb7 This interpretation is mathematically false.
\f1\i0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 with:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f7\i \cf2 \cb7 No interpretation worth investigating could embody the intuition behind it.
\f1\i0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Those are very different assertions.\cf0 \cb1 \
